Leo: Me too. What are you most looking forward to?
Mia: Being able to vote, I think. I want a say in how things are run.
Leo: That''s a good one. For me, it''s getting my driving licence.
Mia: Won''t your mum worry about you on the road?
Leo: A little. But I think I''m mature enough to drive carefully.
Mia: I''m sure you are. Are you nervous about becoming an adult?
Leo: Not really. I know growing up is gradual, not something that happens overnight.', 'Mia 下个月满18岁,十分期待;Leo 也是;Mia 最盼望能投票、对事情有发言权;Leo 最盼望拿驾照;Mia 担心他妈妈会不放心;Leo 说自己够成熟、会小心开车;两人都明白成长是逐渐的,不是一夜之间发生的。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"When is Mia''s eighteenth birthday?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Next month.","Next week.","Tomorrow.","Last year."]},{"q":"What is Mia most looking forward to?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Being able to vote.","Getting a credit card.","Buying a car.","Leaving school."]},{"q":"What is Leo most looking forward to?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Getting his driving licence.","Voting in an election.","Renting a flat.","Starting a new job."]},{"q":"Why isn''t Leo very worried about driving?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["He never makes mistakes.","He feels mature enough to be careful.","His mum will always drive him.","The roads are always empty."]},{"q":"How do both speakers see growing up?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["As something to be afraid of.","As a single event overnight.","As a gradual change, not a sudden one.","As something they cannot control."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'elective2', 'U1', 'fltrp');
This age is often called the age of majority.
At this point, young people can usually vote and sign legal papers.
They also become responsible for choices their parents once made.
Yet many young adults find that real change comes slowly, not overnight.', '在多数国家,年满18岁标志成年的开始;这个年龄常被称为"成年";到此时,年轻人通常可以投票、签署法律文件;他们也开始为从前由父母做的选择负责;但许多年轻人发现,真正的改变是慢慢到来的,而非一夜之间。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"In most countries, what does turning eighteen mark?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["The end of school forever.","The first day of work.","The start of childhood.","The start of adulthood."]},{"q":"What is this age often called?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["The age of majority.","The age of childhood.","The age of retirement.","The age of travel."]},{"q":"What can young people usually do at this age?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Stop obeying every law.","Vote and sign legal papers.","Avoid all responsibility.","Never make a mistake."]},{"q":"What do they become responsible for?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Only their schoolwork.","Nothing at all.","Choices their parents once made.","Their friends'' choices."]},{"q":"What do many young adults discover about change?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["It never happens to anyone.","It happens in a single day.","It only happens to older people.","It comes slowly rather than overnight."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'elective2', 'U1', 'fltrp');
Mr Reed: That''s natural. What worries you most?
Hannah: I''ve never lived away from home. I don''t know how to cook or do laundry.
Mr Reed: Think of it as a chance to learn. You can always ask others for help.
Hannah: I''m also afraid I won''t see my family as much.
Mr Reed: Why not speak to them regularly over the phone or by video call?
Hannah: That''s a good idea. Maybe I''ll join some clubs too, to make new friends.
Mr Reed: Exactly. Living in a group teaches you a lot about growing up.', 'Hannah 担心下周搬进宿舍;Reed 老师说这很正常,问她最担心什么;她从没离家住过,不会做饭和洗衣;老师说把这当作学习的机会,可以向别人求助;她还怕见不到家人;老师建议常打电话或视频;她觉得不错,还打算参加社团交新朋友;老师说集体生活会让人学到很多关于成长的东西。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What is Hannah worried about?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Moving into the dormitory next week.","Failing her driving test.","Losing her part-time job.","Voting for the first time."]},{"q":"Why does she feel unsure about living away?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["She has no money at all.","She cannot cook or do laundry yet.","She dislikes all her classmates.","She has never been to school."]},{"q":"What does Mr Reed suggest about the difficulties?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["She should give up and stay home.","She should keep them secret.","She can treat them as a chance to learn.","She should ignore them completely."]},{"q":"How does Mr Reed suggest she keep in touch with family?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["By moving back home each weekend.","By writing one letter a year.","By never contacting them.","By calling or video-calling them regularly."]},{"q":"What does Hannah plan to do to make new friends?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Join some clubs.","Stay alone in her room.","Leave the dormitory early.","Stop speaking to anyone."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'elective2', 'U1', 'fltrp');
It tells of a pilot who has crashed his plane in the desert.
While he tries to fix it, a little prince from another planet appears.
The two soon become close friends.
The book reminds us to look beneath the surface to find what truly matters.', '《小王子》由法国飞行员安托万·德·圣埃克苏佩里所写;讲述一位飞行员的飞机坠落在沙漠;他修飞机时,一位来自另一星球的小王子出现;两人很快成为好友;这本书提醒我们要看到表象之下,寻找真正重要的东西。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"Who wrote The Little Prince?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["A British librarian.","A French pilot named Saint-Exupéry.","An American teacher.","A Chinese painter."]},{"q":"Where has the pilot in the story crashed?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["In a busy city.","On a high mountain.","In the desert.","At sea."]},{"q":"Who appears while the pilot tries to fix his plane?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["His old teacher.","A police officer.","His worried mother.","A little prince from another planet."]},{"q":"What happens between the two characters?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["They become close friends.","They argue and part forever.","They never speak at all.","They sell the plane together."]},{"q":"What does the book remind readers to do?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Care only about money.","Look beneath the surface for what truly matters.","Forget their childhood quickly.","Trust only what they can see."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'elective2', 'U1', 'fltrp');
Ella: That''s wonderful! How does it feel?
Sam: Amazing. I earned every cent of it at the café this month.
Ella: So, are you going to spend it all at once?
Sam: No way. I''ve decided to save most of it.
Ella: That''s very sensible. What will you do with the rest?
Sam: I''ll give some to help with the household bills at home.
Ella: Your parents will be really proud of you, Sam.', 'Sam 今天拿到第一份工资,十分开心;Ella 替他高兴并问感受;Sam 说很棒,这是他这个月在咖啡馆挣的每一分钱;Ella 问他会不会一下子花光;Sam 说不会,决定把大部分存起来;剩下的会拿一些帮家里付账单;Ella 说他父母一定会为他自豪。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What good news does Sam share?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["He won a free holiday.","He passed his driving test.","He got his first wage today.","He moved into a new flat."]},{"q":"Where did Sam earn the money?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["At a library.","At a hospital.","At a school.","At a café."]},{"q":"What has Sam decided to do with most of the money?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Save most of it.","Spend it all at once.","Give it all away.","Hide it and forget it."]},{"q":"What will Sam do with part of the money?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Buy a new car.","Help pay the household bills.","Travel abroad alone.","Lend it to a stranger."]},{"q":"How does Ella think Sam''s parents will feel?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Angry with him.","Bored by his news.","Really proud of him.","Worried about him."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'elective2', 'U1', 'fltrp');
Real maturity is not only about new freedoms.
It is also about the small, everyday choices you make.
Try to act with integrity, even when no one is watching.
Step by step, these quiet choices shape the person you become.', '给正在成长的人一个简单的小贴士:真正的成熟不只是新获得的自由;它也在于你每天做出的小选择;努力以正直行事,哪怕无人在看;一步步地,这些不起眼的选择塑造你成为什么样的人。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"Who is this tip for?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Only small children.","Only teachers.","Only older people.","Anyone who is growing up."]},{"q":"According to the passage, real maturity is not only about what?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["New freedoms.","Doing well in sport.","Earning lots of money.","Travelling the world."]},{"q":"What else is maturity about?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Avoiding all decisions.","Small, everyday choices.","Pleasing everyone.","Living without rules."]},{"q":"When should you act with integrity?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Only when being rewarded.","Only in front of others.","Even when no one is watching.","Only on special days."]},{"q":"What do these quiet choices do over time?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Make no difference at all.","Bring instant fame.","Waste your time.","Shape the person you become."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'elective2', 'U1', 'fltrp');

